        "id": "ch2_3_1-1",
        "text": "Commands Variable\nSometimes, you might want to execute commands and save their output to a var-\niable. Most of the time, the goal behind this is to manipulate the contents of the\ncommand output. Here\u2019s a simple command that executes the ls command and\nfilters out the filenames that contain the word simple using the grep command.\n(Don\u2019t worry, you will see more complex scenarios in the upcoming sections\nof this chapter. For the time being, practice and focus on the fundamentals.)\n#!/bin/bash\nLS_CMD=$(ls | grep 'simple')\nprintf \"$LS_CMD\\n\"\nHere are the script execution results:\nroot@kali:/opt# simplels.sh\nsimpleadd.sh\nsimplels.sh",
